    pr_ref:  # 4aae
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26 in INV-bamij's third-batch read-back (PR #1237). Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bamij_09262026/ (sherpa-onnx.b3*, crun.b3*).\n\nA call INSIDE a function_definition whose symbol the analyzer did not find emits no calls edge, in c and cpp. Measured by seeding the file anchor everywhere (the first cut of #1237) and classifying every new edge against the parse tree:\n  crun (c):           12 of 18 new edges sat inside a function_definition (e.g. utils.c:2654 xrealloc, exec.c:119 malloc)\n  sherpa-onnx (cpp):  81 of 166 (59 calls, 22 instantiates)\n#1237 deliberately does NOT anchor these on the file (that would hide the gap behind a plausible edge); they stay unemitted, as before.\n\nCAUSE, NOT ESTABLISHED: c looks the function up by position (symbol_declared_by on the function_definition), so a miss means the symbol pass emitted no symbol for that definition; cpp matches by SHORT NAME against local_symbols (`short_name in local_symbols`), so an out-of-class `Foo::bar` definition, an operator, a template specialisation or a same-named overload can miss. Which declarator shapes each language fails on was not read back.\n\nFIX SHAPE: find why each definition has no symbol (or no match) and fix the symbol pass / move cpp to position lookup (INV-midag's rule); then these calls land on their real function."  # 4aae
    fields: {}  # 4aae
- op: discuss  # e42c
  at: '2026-10-01T00:58:26Z'  # e42c
