  clock: 2  # e42c
  nonce: e42c  # e42c
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES -- one cause now established for c and cpp, and cpp also MIS-anchors.\nC CAUSE (repro + source): c.py _get_function_name (c.py:146) and _find_function_declarator (:161) descend ONE pointer_declarator level. A function returning T** (nested pointer_declarator) gets NO symbol, so its calls emit nothing. Scratch fixture: char *one_ptr / char **two_ptr / static char ***three_ptr / int plain, each calling malloc -> symbols+edges only for one_ptr and plain. Both cited crun sites are this shape: utils.c:2654 is in `char **read_dir_entries` (utils.c:2630), exec.c:119 is in `static char **dup_array`. Code dates from 55296f5440 (2026-01-30), not touched since.\nCPP (scratch m.cpp, analyze_cpp):\n  `char **two_ptr(...)` -> no symbol, call unemitted (same nested-pointer shape).\n  `template <> void tpl<int>(int)` -> no symbol, call unemitted.\n  void A::run(){sink(1);} void B::run(){sink(2);} -> BOTH calls anchored on B::run (line 6). over(int)/over(double) -> both calls anchored on the line-12 overload. So the short-name match (cpp.py:1387-1391, `short_name in local_symbols`) does not only MISS: it attributes calls to the WRONG function when two definitions share a short name. operator== and namespace/ref-return shapes worked.\nProposed updates: (1) title/statement add the wrong-anchor half for cpp (finding-relevant, not just recall); (2) fix C's declarator descent recursively (likely the same in cpp's _extract_function_name, cpp.py:418 -- not read); (3) cpp to position lookup per INV-midag -- overlaps WI-tosum (INV-midag residual, cpp listed).\nNot re-measured: crun 12 / sherpa-onnx 81. Not classified: which of the 81 sherpa sites are which shape.\nSide note, not this item: in m.cpp `void sink(int);` is declared in-file yet each call goes to cpp:cstdlib:0-0:sink:unresolved (include attribution); not investigated."  # e42c
- op: update  # 369f
