  set:  # 369f
    title: "c/cpp: a call inside a function definition the analyzer has no symbol for emits no edge (T** returns, cpp template specialisations), and cpp anchors a call on the WRONG same-short-name definition -- crun 12, sherpa-onnx 81 sites"  # 369f
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26 in INV-bamij's third-batch read-back (PR #1237). Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bamij_09262026/ (sherpa-onnx.b3*, crun.b3*).\n\nA call INSIDE a function_definition whose symbol the analyzer did not find emits no calls edge, in c and cpp; and in cpp a call inside a definition whose SHORT NAME another definition in the file shares is anchored on the WRONG function. Measured at filing by seeding the file anchor everywhere (the first cut of #1237) and classifying every new edge against the parse tree (not re-measured 2026-09-30):\n  crun (c):           12 of 18 new edges sat inside a function_definition (e.g. utils.c:2654 xrealloc, exec.c:119 malloc)\n  sherpa-onnx (cpp):  81 of 166 (59 calls, 22 instantiates)\n#1237 deliberately does NOT anchor these on the file (that would hide the gap behind a plausible edge); they stay unemitted.\n\nC CAUSE (established 2026-09-30). c looks the enclosing function up by position (`_get_enclosing_function` -> `symbol_declared_by`, c.py:446), so a miss means the symbol pass emitted no symbol. `_get_function_name` (c.py:146) and `_find_function_declarator` (c.py:161) descend ONE `pointer_declarator` level, so a function returning `T**` or deeper (nested pointer_declarator) gets NO symbol at all, and its calls emit nothing. Repro (analyze_c, scratch m.c): `char *one_ptr`, `char **two_ptr`, `static char ***three_ptr`, `int plain`, each calling malloc -> symbols and edges only for one_ptr and plain. Both cited crun sites are this shape: utils.c:2654 is in `char **read_dir_entries` (utils.c:2630), exec.c:119 is in `static char **dup_array`. Code unchanged since 55296f5440 (2026-01-30). Not checked: other declarator shapes (a function returning a function pointer, parenthesized declarators).\n\nCPP (repro 2026-09-30, analyze_cpp, scratch m.cpp). cpp matches the enclosing definition by SHORT NAME (`short_name in local_symbols`, cpp.py:1387-1391), which keeps one symbol per name:\n  MISSES -- no symbol, call unemitted: `char **two_ptr(...)` (same nested-pointer shape), `template <> void tpl<int>(int)` (explicit specialisation).\n  WRONG ANCHOR -- `void A::run(){sink(1);}` and `void B::run(){sink(2);}`: both calls are anchored on B::run; `over(int)` / `over(double)`: both calls anchored on the second overload. This is a wrong-source edge, not a missing one.\n  Worked: out-of-class `A::operator==`, a namespaced function, a reference-returning function.\nNot classified: which of the 81 sherpa-onnx sites are which shape. Not read: cpp's `_extract_function_name` (cpp.py:418) pointer handling.\n\nFIX SHAPE: (1) c: descend nested pointer_declarators to the function_declarator in `_get_function_name` and `_find_function_declarator` (one helper), and check cpp's name extractor for the same; (2) cpp: emit a symbol for an explicit template specialisation; (3) cpp: find the enclosing function by POSITION (`symbols_at` / `symbol_declared_by`, INV-midag's rule), which fixes the wrong-anchor half; overlaps WI-tosum (INV-midag residual, cpp listed). Then these calls land on their real function.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 369f
- op: discuss  # 163a
  at: '2026-10-01T22:54:27Z'  # 163a
  by: agent  # 163a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 163a
  clock: 4  # 163a
  nonce: 163a  # 163a
  message: "WORKED 2026-10-01 (concurrent run, agent saduj). Local branch jgstern-agent/fix/saduj in ~/hg_wt/saduj, NOT pushed: 7c1e36555c + 92af0129ec.\n\nCHANGE. (1) New shared walk `c_family_declarator` (c.py) follows a definition's declarator chain to the name at any depth, through the unfielded wrappers (parenthesized_declarator, cpp reference_declarator); the innermost function_declarator is the function's own. c and cpp both use it. cpp also names the leaves it had no branch for: explicit specialisation (`template <> void f<int>(int)`, named `f`), operator== (free/friend/member), in-class destructor, conversion operator in and out of class. A function_declarator DIRECTLY inside another (`PFX(x)(args)`, `LUALIB_API int (f)(..)`) and a cpp definition with no function_declarator that is not a conversion operator (`class API X : public MoveOnly<X,Y> {..}`) stay unnamed, as on dev, rather than mint symbols called PFX / int / MoveOnly. (2) cpp finds the enclosing definition by POSITION (symbols_at / symbol_declared_by over file_symbols()), not short name; same for the dispatch-table body scan (c and cpp) and cpp's module_attr_ref anchoring (enclosing_symbols was the name-keyed view).\n\nTESTS. test_c_call_anchor (+3), test_cpp_call_anchor (new, 4). Red before the fix: 5 failed / 131 passed (the 5 then-existing new tests). Final targeted smart-test: 9223 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed; changed files 100%; mypy ratchet clean.\n\nMEASURED (instrument ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/saduj/measure.py; base = git archive of origin/dev, after2 = the branch; module path checked per arm). Call/new sites inside a definition with no symbol, and calls+instantiates edges whose src span does not contain the line:\n  crun (c)        14 -> 0 sites   | out-of-span 0 -> 0\n  tmate (c)       37 -> 26        | 0 -> 0 (26 = compat/tree.h macro bodies)\n  redis (c)       2899 -> 2823    | 0 -> 0 (rest = macro-named defs: jemalloc TEST_BEGIN 2598, fast_float.h C++ parsed as C 210, PFX-style 15)\n  sherpa-onnx     112 -> 3        | 3769+72 -> 0\n  bento4          8 -> 0          | 2228+428 -> 0\n  modsecurity     48 -> 0         | 256+94 -> 0\n  x265            15431 -> 1      | 4558+34 -> 0 (15390 sites were in explicit specialisations, intra_pred<32,30> etc.; calls edges 32940 -> 48306)\n  falco           14 -> 0         | 1906+59 -> 0\nThe cpp out-of-span count is far larger than the 81 filed: the short-name anchor misattributed every overload's and every same-named method's edges, not only the template/T** shapes. A side effect read in the diff: calls TO a newly named function now resolve in-repo (tmate cmd_copy_argv: was c:external unresolved). NOT measured: module_attr_ref re-anchoring on the corpus (attr edge counts are equal per arm; the instrument does not see a read moved off the file anchor), the item's original 12/81 classification with its original instrument, repos other than these eight.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-tikop (macro-named definitions), WI-hilum (cpp callee side: an overload's call to its sibling resolves to one same-name symbol, a false self-call on sherpa-onnx InitKeywords), WI-fohuh (cuda descends no pointer_declarator at all)."  # 163a
