  message: "DONE: merged in PR #1383. analyze_c on a fixture with char *one_ptr, char **two_ptr, static char ***three_ptr, int (*getfn(void))(int), char * const *cptr and int (paren)(int) emits a symbol and the malloc call for every one (dev: one_ptr and plain only). analyze_cpp names char **f, int *&f, template <> void tpl<int>(int) (as tpl), free/friend/member operators, an in-class destructor and a conversion operator, and anchors P::run/Q::run and over(int)/over(double) on their own definitions (dev: both on the last). test_c_call_anchor (+3) and test_cpp_call_anchor (4) red -> green; cpp VERIFIED in test_call_anchor_gate. Corpus (8 repos): missed call sites crun 14->0, sherpa-onnx 112->3, x265 15431->1, bento4/modsecurity/falco ->0; out-of-span calls+instantiates sherpa-onnx 3841->0, bento4 2656->0, x265 4592->0, falco 1965->0, modsecurity 350->0. NOT asserted: no c/cpp definition lacks a symbol (macro-named: WI-tikop). Residuals: WI-fohuh, WI-hilum, WI-rugin (P3).\nFull report (closure evidence, corpus tables, residual list): /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/saduj.md"  # 4c23
